{"id":"000VJ4","title":"Wanderer of the Worldlines (Version 1.0.1)","author":"Kutsumi Hane","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-17T17:33:19+00:00","posted":"Gestern, 18:30 Uhr","rules":"Doesn't look like a bright morning —\n\na thin fog lies over the whole town\n\nBefore the mirror,\n\nsomeone is dressing, straightening their clothes\n\nOutside the window, a hush so deep\n\nthe butterflies beat their wings — as if they have lost their way\n\nDizziness strikes\n\nNo warning at all\n\nThe one at the mirror: no shadow, no trace\n\nOnly the butterflies out the window, still beating their wings\n\n…\n\n— Introduction —\n\nThis is a series of variant Sudokus.\n\nEvery puzzle starts in the same familiar place: a 9×9 grid under standard rules.\n\nEven if you've only dabbled in variant Sudoku, you can jump right in — most puzzles sit comfortably around 2 to 3 stars, with only the final one going a little past 4. All in all, plan for about 10 hours of play.\n\n— Rules —\n\nSudoku — Place the digits 1–9 exactly once in every row, every column, and every 3×3 box.\n\nDynamic Fog — Entering a correct digit into a cell will clear the fog from that cell, and perhaps others.\n\nDynamic Rules —\nSelecting a cell may change the rules the puzzle displays.\n\n⚠ To avoid spoilers, refrain from reading the rules when selecting cells still under fog.\n\nAll further rules reveal themselves in the game.\n\nUnless explicitly stated, negative constraints do not apply.\n\n— Notes —\n\n-\nThe series is fully playable on both desktop and mobile.\n\nHowever, please do not switch devices or browsers mid-series — your progress is saved locally in your browser.\n\nClick the butterfly below to start the first puzzle on\nSudokuPad.\n\nAnd as you go, you'll find your way to the next.\n\nThis series was born from a game I played: Sudokuvania, by Skeptical Mario.\nThe idea took root there and never quite let go of me — until I finally made one of my own.\nThe grids were set in SudokuMaker, built by sirxemic, and are meant to be solved in SudokuPad, created by Sven Neumann;\nThe dynamic rules run on a JSON post-processing script, written by cirne. Without their tools, none of this would have taken shape.\n\nAnd finally — I wish you joyful solving!","solutionCode":"Row 1 of the World with Divergence over 1.0%","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/q5gsv5uz5c","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"link":"https://sudokupad.app/q5gsv5uz5c","linkKind":"sudokupad","attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-17T20:41:39+00:00","settings":{},"summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","underlays"]}}